report=f'''# Rev15V2 — Narrow open steel cypher entrance

A 1.8 m entrance now sits at Y15.1 on the level asphalt beyond the existing navigation stand at Y11. Short pale boundary walls, masonry jambs and coping frame the opening; returns close the ends beside the front houses. A single left-hinged 1.72 m steel leaf opens outwards toward the gully at exactly 90 degrees to the wall. It has 13 vertical 16 mm rods with approximately 10 cm clear gaps, two light cross rails, a square-tube frame, hinge knuckles, wall plates and a latch. There is no opaque panel or raised threshold. The open leaf remains on the left of the walking line.

The new work is six objects (five meshes and a hinge parent) and changes no existing source object. Original geometry, every UV, vertex colour, transform and face material are exact. The coloured Events plaster and all eight posters/frames/heading are retained. The whole Team building, upper windows and all eight exclusive mural states are unchanged. Navigation, the digital sponsor display, other houses, road/potholes, crowd and saved lights are unchanged. No ground railing is reintroduced. Original movement/input/rendering code is unchanged; this is a native environment and runtime-asset change, not a live walkable website integration.

Native master: `{b['editedMaster']}`, {b['editedBytes']:,} bytes, SHA-256 `{b['editedSHA256']}`. Active scene `{b['scene']}` has 58 scenes, retaining all 57 earlier memberships. All resources remain packed. A fresh open and an actual source reconstruction followed by an independent fresh opening pass. A per-face geometry audit confirms no new surface crosses the 1.65 m central corridor, and the leaf lies entirely beyond the navigation stand. The earlier V1 phase separately verified reconstruction from the restored V base.

The parented hinge/leaf fingerprint composes their authored transforms explicitly because newly linked Blender objects can retain a stale matrix cache before reopening. The composed matrices match the independent fresh-open result exactly. Actual saved geometry/angle/clearance checks and the reconstructed-scene fingerprint also pass.

The GLB exports only the new gate/wall component, preserving the parent transform and gate metadata. Chromium loads it without JS, request or GL errors and verifies the single leaf, -90 degree opening, 1.8 m aperture and 13 rods. The browser review uses diagnostic lights/floor and makes no full-world performance or walking-collision claim. Production integration must add this component to the matching full world and retain the narrow entrance corridor in the navigation/collision registry.

[Combined four-page PDF]({pdf['url']}) shows the coloured Events wall, entrance approach, open gate detail and saved night lighting. Neutral inspection views are labelled; inspection lights are never saved. [Drive phase]({phase}). Full-world production integration remains pending. No commit, push or deployment was made. User visual review is pending.

The source checkpoint includes the gate source, runtime/native component, viewer and Three.js license, reports, PDF, captures, hashes and verified base indexes. The full 58-scene native master is recovered from the immutable base chain plus V/V1/V2 source and maps; earlier checkpoints and sharing are preserved. See RESTORE.md.
''';(R/'REPORT.md').write_text(report)
